# Vercel only needs to serve dashboard/ as a static site (see vercel.json's
# outputDirectory). Everything below is the Python side of the project and
# would otherwise get uploaded pointlessly on every deploy.
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.env
.env.example
agent
atlas
benchmark
requirements.txt
README.md

# server.py is the local-dev FastAPI server (live agent calls, /api/claims).
# It must not ship to Vercel: this is a static-only deploy of dashboard/'s
# HTML/CSS/JS/data.js, with no backend and no API key exposed publicly. Its
# presence is what triggers Vercel's "FastAPI entrypoint found" auto-detect.
dashboard/server.py
